if (ret) {
    md_unregister_thread(mddev, &conf->thread);
    if (!mddev->private)
        raid1_free(mddev, conf);
    return ret;
}
Reason:
Adding `md_unregister_thread()` before deallocating `conf` ensures the registered thread is properly cleaned up, preventing the memory leak. This aligns with the error handling in other failure paths of `raid1_run()`.

